From: toktier maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Add a `toktier` tokenizer backend (CPU, per-session reuse)

Adds `--tokenizer-backend toktier`, shaped like the `fastokens` branch:
the tokenizer SGLang loads is wrapped after the post-load fixes, encode
calls run on toktier's certified CPU route (ids equal to a from-scratch
reference encode), and the request's `session_id` (else `cache_salt`) is
bound around the tokenize call so a conversation's transcript is served
as a verified prefix append instead of a full re-encode. With the
adapter's process pool enabled (TOKTIER_SGLANG_SCHED_WORKERS > 0),
`_tokenize_texts` awaits the pool for plain text inputs instead of
encoding on the event loop's thread. No other code path changes.
Requires `toktier >= 0.3.0` (toktier.integrations.sglang).
Baseline: sglang 0.5.21 (PyPI wheel); also applies to 0.5.20.
---
